      "message": "Could this over-redact if the credential value happens to be in the url or payload? Since the credential only ever lives in `argv` we can redact per-token instead by substring. \n```\ndef redact(argv, secrets):\n    secret_set \u003d set(filter(None, secrets))\n    return \" \".join(REDACTED if token in secret_set else token for token in argv)\n```\n\nOr better to move it to `CurlAuth` so the object that knows which tokens are secret is the one that masks them:\n```\n@property\ndef redacted_argv(self) -\u003e List\n    secret_set \u003d set(filter(None, self.secrets))\n    return [REDACTED if token in secret_set else token for token in self.argv]\n```",
